From 596efafd9017c6a03ecfbf3b59e239aea7f8bd6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 02:13:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/44] feat(chexc): capability parameter inference (proposal
 6.3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Non-exported declarations without an authoritative clause get their capability
lists inferred from their bodies, as the least solution of

    C(f) = local(f) ∪ ⋃ over call sites: (C(callee) ∖ discharged at the site)

- The subtraction needs no separate representation: the checking walker already
  reports exactly the demands its supply stack fails to discharge, so running it
  in collect mode against each callee's current list computes one iteration of
  the equations. Iterating to stability yields the least fixpoint; monotonicity
  guarantees termination. Discharge by an enclosing try-catch and by a function
  literal whose expected type carries the capability both fall out of the shared
  supply logic (6.3.2).
- Eligibility (6.3.1): has a body, not public/protected, not an interface member,
  and either no clause or one ending in '...'; 'main' excluded.
- Tarjan SCC over the intra-package call graph; components come out callee-first,
  which is the bottom-up order of 6.3.3. Members are processed in declaration
  order for reproducible diagnostics.
- Polymorphic recursion (6.3.4) is rejected by an occurs check on call type
  arguments, with a dedicated diagnostic naming the growing instantiation.
- Inferred lists live beside the AST (InferredCapabilities) rather than in
  declaration types: checking stays a pure check, and call sites resolve a
  callee's list through the map since their types were formed during Sema.
- Parser: '...' is accepted in declaration clauses (still rejected in functional
  types, whose lists are complete) and hashed for incremental correctness.
- Capability lists are now preserved through two more type reconstruction sites
  (UnsolvedAsQuest, TyGeneralizer::Generalize): they take no part in inference
  (3.6) but must survive it, since a literal checked against such a type inherits
  them (3.5).

Gate: CheckedExceptions inference 6/6, parse 11/11, types 10/10, scopes 7/7,
captures 6/6, unchecked 4/4; ctest 49/49; Parser/Sema LLT 3934/3934; fmt clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
